# Titan Orbit — Toroidal map

The playable map is a **torus on XZ**: leaving one edge wraps to the opposite. Ships **do not teleport** at seams; presentation and gameplay use different math. Paired: `ToroidalMapEcs`, `ToroidalDisplay`, ship-simulation rule. Deep dive: `Docs/TITAN-ORBIT-COMPLETE-COURSE.md` §11.4.

---

## Two layers (do not mix)

| Layer | Behavior | API |
|-------|----------|-----|
| **Sim / gameplay** | Ships fly **unbounded** (no wrap of owner hull). Distances, docking, orbit, combat, beams, transports use **shortest path on the torus**. | `ToroidalMapEcs.ShortestOffsetXZ`, `ToroidalDistance`, `ToroidalDirection` |
| **Presentation** | Local ship stays put in world space; each planet/asteroid/remote picks its own nearest **map-tile copy** (+ hysteresis). | `ToroidalMapEcs.GetDisplayPosition*`, `ToroidalDisplay` |

```csharp
// ❌ BAD — Euclidean distance across the seam (misses / false “far”)
float d = math.distance(ship.xz, planet.xz);

// ✅ GOOD — toroidal shortest path
float d = ToroidalMapEcs.ToroidalDistance(ship, planet, mapW, mapH);

// ❌ BAD — wrap local ship LocalTransform at edge (global blink / retile storm)
transform.Position = ToroidalMapEcs.Wrap(transform.Position);

// ✅ GOOD — leave ship unbounded; retile *other* bodies for display only
displayPos = ToroidalMapEcs.GetDisplayPosition(logicalPos, localShipPos, mapW, mapH);
```

`Wrap` exists for canonicalization when needed — **not** the ship flight path.

---

## Feature checklist (orbit, dock, transports, combat)

Any new range / target / spawn / magnet / orbit / unload logic must:

- [ ] Read `mapW` / `mapH` from `MapStateSingleton` (or `ToroidalMapEcs` after bootstrap)
- [ ] Use **toroidal** distance/offset/direction — never raw `distance` on XZ for gameplay
- [ ] Place moons / surface spawns with **near-tile** helpers (`GetMoonWorldPositionNear`, surface-toward that uses shortest offset)
- [ ] Keep presentation on `ToroidalDisplay` / display helpers — do not drive sim from display tiles
- [ ] Cross-seam hull contact: prefer `ShipToroidalWorldCollision*` patterns, not assuming PhysX sees both sides

**Orbit ring / people transport:** ring membership = `PlanetOrbitMath.IsInOrbitRing(ToroidalDistance(...), inner, outer)`. Tangents use `ShortestOffsetXZ(planet → ship)` so clockwise orbit works across seams.

---

## Forbidden

- Euclidean-only gameplay ranges on a wrapped map
- Wrapping the **local** predicted ship transform to “fix” the seam
- One global map snap that retiles every body when the owner crosses an edge
- Hard-coded map size ignoring `MapStateSingleton` / session meta

## Agent checklist

- [ ] Gameplay math is toroidal
- [ ] Ship sim stays unbounded
- [ ] Display is per-body nearest tile (+ hysteresis where used)
- [ ] New systems document mapW/mapH sources in comments
